tests/smoke -- the shortest check
=================================

    make test                    build legion's firmware set from this tree
                                 (cached by a hash of the tree: an unchanged
                                 tree is not rebuilt), then the check below
    tests/smoke/run FWDIR        the check alone on a set you already have
                                 (FWDIR from `make all TARGET=legion`, or
                                 any directory with reset.bin q.bin openboot.bin
                                 nvram1 1up-md.bin 1up-hv.bin)
    make test-full               test + everything in tests/full (the
                                 maintainer's full set); `make tests-full` is
                                 the same

It boots the set under QEMU and requires two things in the console output: the
banner ("Sun Fire T2000") and, after it, OpenBoot's `ok` prompt as the last
non-empty line. That is all. The banner header (name and memory, copyright,
OpenBoot version, Ethernet address, Host ID) is printed for a human but not
compared: a changed version or serial would only give a red test nobody can
judge. What the banner says is checked against the MD in tests/full/boot
(`make boot-verify`), together with the device tree and its properties.
About 1.5 seconds once the firmware exists.

A hypervisor that rejects its MD prints nothing at all, so "no banner" is the
failure you see when the MD, hv and OpenBoot do not fit together; a banner
without the ok prompt means OpenBoot started and did not finish. What it does
not say: which configuration it was (any of them prints "Sun Fire T2000"),
which OpenBoot build, or anything about the tree, properties or Solaris.

Needs qemu-system-sparc from the distribution (`apt install
qemu-system-sparc`, REQUIREMENTS.LINUX), or run it in a container (container/).
